window.products.push({"id":100443,"name":"EFP Humidifier Filters for 1041 Aircare Essick Air Bemis Model Humidifiers Replacement Wicking Filters | Includes 2 Aftermarket Filters…","category":"homeandappliances","retail price":33.99,"sale price":null,"image":"https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51csjQhw3lL._AC_SL1000_.jpg","description":"EFP Replacement Humidifier Wicking Filters Compatible with 1041 Aircare Essick Air Bemis Model Humidifiers | Includes 2 High Quality, Aftermarket Filters SIX PACK: Includes 6 High Quality Aftermarket Replacement EFP Humidifier Wick Filters for 1041 Aircare Essick Air Bemis Model Humidifiers. Approximate Measurements: 16-5/8 x 9-7/8 x 5. Replacing your humidifier filter regularly ensures that harmful particles are removed from the water before it is released into the air. EFP High Output Interwoven Filter Designs help trap and retain mineral deposits for natural and clean humidification - No White Dust. EFP provides High Quality Replacement Parts that are a guaranteed Exact Fit and Affordably Priced compared to the OEM product. This is a high quality EFP Brand Replacement Part. ~Quality, Fit, and Workmanship are Fully Guaranteed. We offer a No-Hassle 30 -Day Money Back Guarantee on all EFP products so you can be confident in your purchase decision. Why should you replace your humidifier Filter? A humidifier is an essential household appliance, particularly for the winter months when the air becomes a lot drier and less humid. Your humidifier helps by dispersing water vapor into the air to replace the lost moisture. Most humidifiers contain filters, which help to keep the moist air clear of any impurities. They remove particles from the water before it is dispensed into the air. You need to change your filters regularly, so you can continue to enjoy healthy air and keep your humidifier in good condition. The frequency of changing depends on the quality of your household water supply and how often you are using the humidifier. There are many different types of humidifier filters. Check your user manual or the manufacturers website to make sure you know what type you need to buy.","images":["https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51csjQhw3lL._AC_SL1000_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61zNIJh6ZCL._SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/61TWUez1VxL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51TIpnkrEpL._AC_SL1500_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/51I6jTu8yCL._AC_SL1300_.jpg","https://m.media-amazon.com/images/I/31o9GyU6jnL._AC_.jpg"],"specifications":{"brand":"EFP","source_asin":"B0BP4CPDX3","category_path":"Home & Appliances"},"sku":"BM-100443","productType":"Home & Appliances","inventory":0,"age_group":"Adult","gender":"Unisex","source_url":"https://www.amazon.com/dp/B0BP4CPDX3","source_catalog":"Amazon Reviews 2023 product metadata","source_file":"meta_Appliances.jsonl","source_asin":"B0BP4CPDX3","price_pending":true,"merchant_ready":false});
